(3124841, 437699, 66201, '<td valign="top">Really good clarity and crispness for such low light - well done.I love the slight movement blur on her hand while the rest of her is so still. The bubbling pot alos gives this the little bit of energy it needs.9</td>', 'Really good clarity and crispness for such low light - well done.I love the slight movement blur on her hand while the rest of her is so still. The bubbling pot alos gives this the little bit of energy it needs.9', '2006-12-17 01:13:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3124858, 437739, 66201, '<td valign="top">Really lovely natural capture. I like the "real life" aspect to this. Maybe I''m just so used to colour saturation in pictures in these challenges, and am looking for redder and greener fruits, but at the same time, the lack of saturation is refreshing. The woman is the focal point and she is expertly treated in terms of focus and texture. I like her placement on the right hand side.</td>', 'Really lovely natural capture. I like the "real life" aspect to this. Maybe I''m just so used to colour saturation in pictures in these challenges, and am looking for redder and greener fruits, but at the same time, the lack of saturation is refreshing. The woman is the focal point and she is expertly treated in terms of focus and texture. I like her placement on the right hand side.', '2006-12-17 01:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3124871, 437905, 66201, '<td valign="top">Fantastic subject: so unique.If I had to offer any "what I would have done" comment, I think it would be that a tighter crop on the right might have been a better option... I know that you would have had to sacrifice the gorgeous Celtic Knot design on the fabric then, but that would have made the fletcher a wee bit more Primary. Hmm...but I like it as it is too. 9</td>', 'Fantastic subject: so unique.If I had to offer any "what I would have done" comment, I think it would be that a tighter crop on the right might have been a better option... I know that you would have had to sacrifice the gorgeous Celtic Knot design on the fabric then, but that would have made the fletcher a wee bit more Primary. Hmm...but I like it as it is too. 9', '2006-12-17 01:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
