(3135553, 438086, 66384, '<td valign="top">Very clever to have changed the odd pepper to green. I would never have thought of that. That''s the difference between a good photographer and an artist and ribbon winner. BTW, I do not agree with those comments that said the color and exposure aren''t right. They look perfect on my monitor. Congratulations on your well deserved blue!</td>', 'Very clever to have changed the odd pepper to green. I would never have thought of that. That''s the difference between a good photographer and an artist and ribbon winner. BTW, I do not agree with those comments that said the color and exposure aren''t right. They look perfect on my monitor. Congratulations on your well deserved blue!', '2006-12-20 12:13:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3135795, 437796, 51802, '<td valign="top">I think this is a great idea, but the perspective is what hurts this shot.  The columns and the lights at the top are a big distraction and make it a little too busy.  It might have worked better if you were in the same room as the bar.  It would be interesting to see all the bottles against their colored background with the silhouettes of the people in front of them.</td>', 'I think this is a great idea, but the perspective is what hurts this shot.  The columns and the lights at the top are a big distraction and make it a little too busy.  It might have worked better if you were in the same room as the bar.  It would be interesting to see all the bottles against their colored background with the silhouettes of the people in front of them.', '2006-12-20 13:10:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3135798, 437796, 16488, '<td valign="top">I like the patterns of color in this image. The dark mood of the bar seduces me. I wish this image delivered more in the silhouettes...were the profiles more distinctive, the heads turned a bit more toward each other, I might have felt the subjects connecting more strongly to each other and, by extension, to me as the viewer. Were I cropping this, I would have trimmed the black window frame(?) from the left so that it would balance with the open colors on the right...then cropped up a bit from the bottom as there is no real need for the extra black nor that annoying little object in the lower left.<br/> <br/>--comment left per request in <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=514236" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this thread.</a></td>', 'I like the patterns of color in this image. The dark mood of the bar seduces me. I wish this image delivered more in the silhouettes...were the profiles more distinctive, the heads turned a bit more toward each other, I might have felt the subjects connecting more strongly to each other and, by extension, to me as the viewer. Were I cropping this, I would have trimmed the black window frame(?) from the left so that it would balance with the open colors on the right...then cropped up a bit from the bottom as there is no real need for the extra black nor that annoying little object in the lower left. --comment left per request in this thread.', '2006-12-20 13:11:10.000000', NULL, 0),
