(3136131, 438086, 28141, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot.  The contrast is excellent and it''s very eye catching.  I would have thought that changing the color of the pepper like that would be pushing the major elements rule a little too far (though I haven''t had time to properly review the new rules), but if it''s not, then that''s good to know for future challenges :-).  Congrats!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-20 14:21:34.</i></td>', 'I really like this shot.  The contrast is excellent and it''s very eye catching.  I would have thought that changing the color of the pepper like that would be pushing the major elements rule a little too far (though I haven''t had time to properly review the new rules), but if it''s not, then that''s good to know for future challenges :-).  Congrats!', '2006-12-20 14:53:18.000000', '2007-08-20 15:21:34.000000', 0),
(3136136, 436589, 69350, '<td valign="top">Thank you to all those who stopped by, commented or voted. Much appreciated. :)</td>', 'Thank you to all those who stopped by, commented or voted. Much appreciated. :)', '2006-12-20 14:55:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136138, 436589, 69350, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by alexsaberi:</b></div><hr/><i> like this one. nice processing 8 </i></td></tr></table> <br/>An 8 from you is already a gift as you are one of the great ones here in DPC. Thank you. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by alexsaberi: like this one. nice processing 8  An 8 from you is already a gift as you are one of the great ones here in DPC. Thank you. :)', '2006-12-20 14:56:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136157, 436742, 53316, '<td valign="top">Leaving aside the background, I think there are a couple things here. I would have liked to see all of his head in the frame, and the shadows cast by the right arm  and the ear are a bit harsh.  Other than that though I really liked this shot (and really I only noticed those things because I was looking for things that might have been "off" as you said).  Like bmartuch''s comment mentioned, there is a lot of emotion here - that was the first thing I noticed when I came across this image.  I also really like the title - long titles have a way of being cheesy sometimes but that is not the case here.  The title really brings things home for the viewer as far as connecting the visual to the challenge and also giving the boy some personality (by way of how you phrased the title).</td>', 'Leaving aside the background, I think there are a couple things here. I would have liked to see all of his head in the frame, and the shadows cast by the right arm  and the ear are a bit harsh.  Other than that though I really liked this shot (and really I only noticed those things because I was looking for things that might have been "off" as you said).  Like bmartuch''s comment mentioned, there is a lot of emotion here - that was the first thing I noticed when I came across this image.  I also really like the title - long titles have a way of being cheesy sometimes but that is not the case here.  The title really brings things home for the viewer as far as connecting the visual to the challenge and also giving the boy some personality (by way of how you phrased the title).', '2006-12-20 15:04:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136223, 436742, 50641, '<td valign="top">This is really nice, so sorry about the dq.  I love the composition - eyes follow body and lines right to the rose.  <br/> <br/>Lighting is great.  I might possibly reduce the saturation of the reds in his face a tiny bit.  The yellow and green against the black shirt really works well. <br/> <br/>Maybe you would consider posting the original?  Am very curious about the background now. It''s so hard to tell how much is too much when it comes to this sort of thing.<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is really nice, so sorry about the dq.  I love the composition - eyes follow body and lines right to the rose.   Lighting is great.  I might possibly reduce the saturation of the reds in his face a tiny bit.  The yellow and green against the black shirt really works well.  Maybe you would consider posting the original?  Am very curious about the background now. It''s so hard to tell how much is too much when it comes to this sort of thing. ', '2006-12-20 15:20:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136228, 437470, 57429, '<td valign="top">Nice picture.  Thank you</td>', 'Nice picture.  Thank you', '2006-12-20 15:22:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136531, 437739, 48890, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  A very nice candid shot.</td>', 'Congratulations!  A very nice candid shot.', '2006-12-20 16:48:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136584, 437470, 48890, '<td valign="top">As much as I love to see candid photographs as top finishers in any challenge, I don''t like this picture.  What you did to the colours is atrocious, and the composition is too up-front and messy.</td>', 'As much as I love to see candid photographs as top finishers in any challenge, I don''t like this picture.  What you did to the colours is atrocious, and the composition is too up-front and messy.', '2006-12-20 17:00:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136595, 438086, 5112, '<td valign="top">Many congratulations on your first ribbon!</td>', 'Many congratulations on your first ribbon!', '2006-12-20 17:01:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136596, 437649, 48890, '<td valign="top">Not bad!</td>', 'Not bad!', '2006-12-20 17:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
